<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Nop.Web.SmokeTests - the ASP.NET Core host smoke check, created by task 7.7
    (Requirements 4.1, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5, 4.6, 1.4).

    WHY THIS PROJECT EXISTS
    =======================
    Task groups 2-7 were validated by COMPILATION ONLY. Apart from the 4 fixtures in
    src/Tests/Nop.Tests, no ported line of this migration had ever been EXECUTED before
    this project, and roughly 40 entries in .kiro/specs/dotnetmodernization/runtime-deferrals.md
    are recorded as RESOLVED on the strength of code inspection or of throwaway probes run
    against synthetic host applications. This project runs the real thing.

    It boots the REAL Nop.Web host through WebApplicationFactory<Nop.Web.Program>: the real
    Program.Main, builder.Environment.UseNopHostingEnvironment(...), the real
    AddNopFramework() service graph, the real Autofac container built by NopHostedEngine, the
    real middleware pipeline in the real order, and the real compiled Razor views. Requests go
    through TestServer rather than a socket, so no port is bound and nothing is left running.

    NON-GATING, deliberately. tasks.md marks 7.7 non-gating and the migration's completion
    criterion remains Clean_Compile (Requirement 3.3). A failure here is a finding to record,
    not a build break - which is why this project is NOT added to any gate command.

    TARGET FRAMEWORK / SDK
    ======================
    Microsoft.NET.Sdk, not Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web: this is a test assembly, not a web
    application. The ASP.NET Core surface it needs
    (Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http, .Mvc, .Builder, .Routing, .TestHost) arrives through the
    Microsoft.AspNetCore.App FrameworkReference that Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing adds
    implicitly, so no explicit FrameworkReference is declared here (restating it would fail
    with NETSDK1086, the same trap Nop.Web.csproj documents).

    TargetFramework, Nullable, ImplicitUsings and GenerateAssemblyInfo come from
    src/Directory.Build.props; net10.0 is restated so it is verifiable from this file
    (Requirement 1.2). There is no Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs - this is a new project, not a
    converted one, so there is no hand-kept file to preserve and nothing is lost by
    GenerateAssemblyInfo=false.

    PACKAGES
    ========
    Versions come from src/Directory.Packages.props (ManagePackageVersionsCentrally=true,
    CentralPackageVersionOverrideEnabled=false), so every item is intentionally version-less.
    The test-SDK trio matches the pattern task 4.5 established for src/Tests/Nop.Tests -
    NUnit is pinned at 3.14.0 there because NUnit 4 removed the classic Assert.AreEqual
    surface, and this project uses the same pin for consistency even though it is new code.

      Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing  WebApplicationFactory<T> + TestServer. The one new
                                        central pin task 7.7 added (10.0.12, aligned with the
                                        other 10.0.12 Microsoft pins).
      Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk            VSTest host - on .NET the runner is a package.
      NUnit / NUnit3TestAdapter         framework + VSTest adapter.

    No mocking package: this project mocks NOTHING on purpose. Every assertion runs against
    the real host, because a smoke check that substitutes a double for the thing under test
    proves nothing about it.

    PROJECT REFERENCES
    ==================
    Nop.Web is referenced so WebApplicationFactory can find its entry point and so the tests
    can name Nop.Web types (Program, NopHostedEngine). The four upstream projects arrive
    transitively; Nop.Core is ALSO declared directly because the tests bind Nop.Core types
    (CommonHelper, EngineContext, ContainerManager, NopConfig, PluginManager,
    DataSettingsHelper) independently of Nop.Web, and the migration's own rule is that direct
    usage means a direct reference.

    NOT referenced: Nop.Admin. Task 7.7's scope boundary is explicit - nothing under
    Administration/ is touched, that is group 8. One consequence IS asserted here, as a
    known-gap test: the install page links admin CSS which does not serve (deferral 7.4-2).
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>

    <!--
      Suppress the NUnit1032 analyzer only where it fires on the shared WebApplicationFactory
      field, which is disposed in OneTimeTearDown rather than per-test. Kept narrow and
      explicit rather than blanket-disabling analyzers.
    -->
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NUnit1032</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" />
    <PackageReference Include="NUnit" />
    <PackageReference Include="NUnit3TestAdapter" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web\Nop.Web.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Core\Nop.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
